      "id": "claim_e19d4b23db1e4328b433cbefa5c6c8b4",
      "statement": "Version pinning is deliberate at behavior-critical seams: fastwebsockets is exactly =0.8.1 because the peer tunnel needs the unstable-split read/write halves (a WebSocket read is not cancel-safe and must survive concurrent writes); sqlite-vec is pinned to the audited C amalgamation =0.1.9; v8 is 152.1 because shared isolates require v8::Locker and Send Globals shipped there; several crypto crates follow deno's ext/node_crypto versions and features.",
